1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,227
A poster looks beautiful,

2
00:00:02,227 --> 00:00:03,786
but its shop name is wrong.

3
00:00:03,786 --> 00:00:04,676
Would you call that

4
00:00:04,676 --> 00:00:07,794
a successful image generation?

5
00:00:07,794 --> 00:00:11,310
Qwen-Image addresses two challenges:

6
00:00:11,310 --> 00:00:12,975
rendering text correctly,

7
00:00:12,975 --> 00:00:15,565
and preserving other content during local edits.

8
00:00:15,565 --> 00:00:16,300
First,

9
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:19,726
a multimodal language model reads the prompt.

10
00:00:19,726 --> 00:00:21,195
When editing an image,

11
00:00:21,195 --> 00:00:23,153
it also interprets the source image,

12
00:00:23,153 --> 00:00:24,866
forming semantic conditions.

13
00:00:24,866 --> 00:00:26,494
A variational autoencoder,

14
00:00:26,494 --> 00:00:28,121
or VAE,

15
00:00:28,121 --> 00:00:30,678
compresses the image into a latent representation.

16
00:00:30,678 --> 00:00:31,375
Finally,

17
00:00:31,375 --> 00:00:34,862
its decoder converts the latent back into pixels.

18
00:00:34,862 --> 00:00:40,712
The multimodal diffusion Transformer receives
semantic conditions and image representations,

19
00:00:40,712 --> 00:00:44,027
and repeatedly predicts how the current state should change.

20
00:00:44,027 --> 00:00:44,997
During training,

21
00:00:44,997 --> 00:00:47,665
a clean image latent

22
00:00:47,665 --> 00:00:50,333
is mixed with random noise according to time.

23
00:00:50,333 --> 00:00:54,214
The model learns the velocity from noise to image.

24
00:00:54,214 --> 00:00:56,089
Suppose the clean value is 2,

25
00:00:56,089 --> 00:00:57,495
the noise is −1,

26
00:00:57,495 --> 00:00:59,369
and time is 0.25.

27
00:00:59,369 --> 00:01:02,181
The interpolated value is −0.25,

28
00:01:02,181 --> 00:01:03,821
and the target velocity is 3.

29
00:01:03,821 --> 00:01:06,568
If the model predicts a velocity of 2.5,

30
00:01:06,568 --> 00:01:09,086
the squared error is 0.25.

31
00:01:09,086 --> 00:01:11,375
This is a one-dimensional teaching example,

32
00:01:11,375 --> 00:01:13,893
not an actual model result.

33
00:01:13,893 --> 00:01:17,004
At inference, the target image is not available.

34
00:01:17,004 --> 00:01:18,918
The model starts from noise,

35
00:01:18,918 --> 00:01:21,072
repeatedly predicts the direction of update,

36
00:01:21,072 --> 00:01:23,704
and finally the decoder reconstructs the image.

37
00:01:23,704 --> 00:01:25,079
When editing a source image,

38
00:01:25,079 --> 00:01:27,599
the semantic path interprets the requested change,

39
00:01:27,599 --> 00:01:30,577
while the visual encoding path supplies source details.

40
00:01:30,577 --> 00:01:33,785
Together, they help with editing and preservation.

41
00:01:33,785 --> 00:01:34,953
The authors report

42
00:01:34,953 --> 00:01:37,523
high accuracy on common Chinese characters,

43
00:01:37,523 --> 00:01:42,428
but only 6.48% on level-three rare characters.

44
00:01:42,428 --> 00:01:45,778
A small lead in scores does not establish statistical significance.

45
00:01:45,778 --> 00:01:48,681
To isolate the contribution of each editing path,

46
00:01:48,681 --> 00:01:52,254
we need ablations with controlled data and compute.

47
00:01:52,254 --> 00:01:53,446
Back to the poster:

48
00:01:53,446 --> 00:01:54,877
looking good is not enough.

49
00:01:54,877 --> 00:01:57,978
We must also check whether the text is correct,

50
00:01:57,978 --> 00:02:00,125
whether the edit follows the request,

51
00:02:00,125 --> 00:02:02,749
and whether the remaining content is preserved.

52
00:02:02,749 --> 00:02:03,910
Remember four steps:

53
00:02:03,910 --> 00:02:05,072
understand the instruction,

54
00:02:05,072 --> 00:02:06,233
represent the image,

55
00:02:06,233 --> 00:02:07,395
predict velocity,

56
00:02:07,395 --> 00:02:08,556
and decode the result.

57
00:02:08,556 --> 00:02:11,576
The paper results are reported by its authors;

58
00:02:11,576 --> 00:02:13,899
the animation uses illustrative numbers.
